/rails/rails/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/deployments","created_at":"2008-04-11T02:19:47Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T07:43:35Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-13T03:40:43Z","git_url":"git://github.com/rails/rails.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:rails/rails.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/rails/rails.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/rails/rails","homepage":"https://rubyonrails.org","size":275235,"stargazers_count":57965,"watchers_count":57965,"language":"Ruby","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":22063,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1385,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["activejob","activerecord","framework","html","mvc","rails","ruby"],"visibility":"public","forks":22063,"open_issues":1385,"watchers":57965,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Ruby 2.2.1 and Rails 4.2.1 (don't know about older versions and master).\n\nI created an app that reproduce the issue: https://github.com/andreynering/controller_test_bug\n\nTake a look at [these tests](https://github.com/andreynering/controller_test_bug/blob/master/test/controllers/comments_controller_test.rb). Just the [last one](https://github.com/andreynering/controller_test_bug/blob/master/test/controllers/comments_controller_test.rb#L32-40) fails. I think it shouldn't.\n\nThis is the error thrown:\n\n``` bash\n$ bin/rake test\nRun options: --seed 63986\n\n# Running:\n\n..E.\n\nFinished in 0.468636s, 8.5354 runs/s, 6.4016 assertions/s.\n\n  1) Error:\nCommentsControllerTest#test_should_create_post_(json_2):\nActiveRecord::StatementInvalid: SQLite3::ConstraintException: NOT NULL constraint failed: comments.post_id: INSERT INTO \"comments\" (\"text\") VALUES (?)\n    app/controllers/comments_controller.rb:35:in `block in create'\n    app/controllers/comments_controller.rb:34:in `create'\n    test/controllers/comments_controller_test.rb:34:in `block (2 levels) in <class:CommentsControllerTest>'\n    test/controllers/comments_controller_test.rb:33:in `block in <class:CommentsControllerTest>'\n\n4 runs, 3 assertions, 0 failures, 1 errors, 0 skips\n```\n\n[Debbugging the `params` hash](https://github.com/andreynering/controller_test_bug/blob/master/app/controllers/comments_controller.rb#L30), I noticed that `post_id` have a Post object (only for the failing test):\n\n``` ruby\n{\"comment\"=>{\"text\"=>\"foo\", \"post_id\"=>#<Post id: 980190962, title: \"MyString\", text: \"MyText\">}, \"format\"=>\"json\", \"controller\"=>\"comments\", \"action\"=>\"create\"}\n```\n\nBut the expected value is the `id` of the post as a string (right?).\n\nThe `params`hash in the other tests:\n\n``` ruby\n{\"comment\"=>{\"text\"=>\"foo\", \"post_id\"=>\"980190962\"}, \"controller\"=>\"comments\", \"action\"=>\"create\"}\n```\n\nIf [in the second test](https://github.com/andreynering/controller_test_bug/blob/master/test/controllers/comments_controller_test.rb#L17) the AR object is converted to the `id`, I think it should happen in the last too.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/19516/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/19516/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]